WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:07.240
As Counselor Deanna Troi on the sci-fi TV
series Star Trek: The Next Generation, British-American

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:13.459
actor Marina Sirtis played one of the most
iconic female characters in the Star Trek

00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:14.080
franchise.

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:19.260
Keep watching to catch up with this talented
actress and find out what she's up to today.

00:00:19.780 --> 00:00:21.220
To boldly go

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:27.810
Although Next Generation came to a close in
1994, that wasn't the end of Sirtis' work

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:28.960
with the Federation.

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:34.800
She reprised her role as Counselor Troi in
all four Next Generation films alongside much

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:37.160
of the original Next Generation cast.

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:44.000
Troi also popped up in three episodes of Star
Trek: Voyager from 1999 to 2000, and also

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:50.610
in the 2005 series finale of Star Trek: Enterprise,
marking her last appearance as Deanna Troi.

00:00:50.610 --> 00:00:55.350
Though with the planned return of Captain
Jean-Luc Picard in a new Star Trek series

00:00:55.350 --> 00:00:58.200
on the horizon, can she be too far behind?

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:00.880
"HE'S BACK!"

00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:08.980
Gargoyles

00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:15.300
After The Next Generation, Sirtis began voice
acting, joining the cast of the Disney animated

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:16.640
series Gargoyles.

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:23.219
From 1994 to 1996, Sirtis voiced Demona, a
villain with a thirst for vengeance against

00:01:23.219 --> 00:01:25.590
the humans that slaughtered her clan.

00:01:25.590 --> 00:01:30.880
While many fans who approach Sirtis at conventions
are fans of her work in both Star Trek and

00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:36.160
Gargoyles, she says that quite a few prefer
Demona over the more "passive" Deanna.

00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:41.740
Sirtis wasn't the only Next Generation actor
that ended up on Gargoyles; Jonathan Frakes

00:01:41.759 --> 00:01:47.819
appeared as David Xanatos, Michael Dorn played
Coldstone, and Brent Spiner voiced Puck.

00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:49.140
That wasn't the end, though.

00:01:49.300 --> 00:01:53.880
She provided the voice of antagonist "Queen
Bee" and several other characters in the Cartoon

00:01:53.889 --> 00:01:59.780
Network animated series Young Justice, and
a dog warrior on Adventure Time, among other

00:01:59.780 --> 00:02:01.380
shows and video games.

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:04.720
"The stars have paired you with a goddess."

00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:07.560
"I like the way you talk, but you are crazy."

00:02:07.640 --> 00:02:15.020
Notably, Sirtis played Matriarch Benezia in
2007's Mass Effect, and most recently Elena

00:02:15.020 --> 00:02:19.320
Dragunova in 2014's XCOM 2: War of the Chosen.

00:02:19.720 --> 00:02:20.980
Back to sci-fi

00:02:21.660 --> 00:02:26.840
After taking some time away from traditional
sci-fi with roles in mystery-themed productions

00:02:26.840 --> 00:02:32.680
like Gadgetman and Diagnosis: Murder, Sirtis
returned to science fiction in 1999 with a

00:02:32.680 --> 00:02:35.700
role in the Showtime series The Outer Limits.

00:02:35.700 --> 00:02:41.110
In "The Grell," Sirtis plays Liv Kohler, whose
family finds themselves in a moral quandary

00:02:41.110 --> 00:02:46.980
when their alien slave demonstrates an unexpected
loyalty to them, forcing her and her husband

00:02:46.980 --> 00:02:49.360
to rethink their bigoted worldview.

00:02:49.640 --> 00:02:55.050
In 2000, Sirtis made an appearance in another
popular science fiction franchise when she

00:02:55.050 --> 00:03:01.600
guest-starred as Russian scientist Dr. Svetlana
Markov in the Stargate SG-1 episode "Watergate."

00:03:01.780 --> 00:03:08.000
In the episode, Markov struggles with a broken
Stargate, body-controlling aliens, and a mysteriously

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:08.640
murdered crew.

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:11.620
Of course, it's nothing that Deanna Troi hasn't
seen before.

00:03:13.620 --> 00:03:14.820
"Pain!

00:03:15.680 --> 00:03:16.980
Such pain!"

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:21.740
She followed this up with a couple of guest
spots in the British hospital drama Casualty,

00:03:21.740 --> 00:03:23.540
and its spin-off series, Holby City.

00:03:23.780 --> 00:03:24.940
But that wasn't all.

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:30.600
She also picked up brief roles in a variety
of American TV shows, but before long, it

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:32.380
was back to sci-fi again.

00:03:32.540 --> 00:03:34.960
Annihilation Earth and beyond

00:03:35.100 --> 00:03:41.960
In 2009, Sirtis landed a starring role in
the SyFy movie Annihilation Earth, as Paxton,

00:03:41.970 --> 00:03:47.240
the leader of a secretive U.N energy project
called EVE, whose decisions will determine

00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:48.560
the fate of the mankind.

00:03:48.700 --> 00:03:51.740
Again, not too far from Troi's deep space
adventures.

00:03:56.500 --> 00:04:01.560
In 2015, she appeared in the investigative
thriller, A Dark Reflection, a British indie

00:04:01.560 --> 00:04:06.650
film directed and produced by former British
Airways pilot Tristan Loraine in order to

00:04:06.650 --> 00:04:11.780
expose an alleged cover-up involving toxic
cabin air in commercial jets.

00:04:12.020 --> 00:04:13.160
NCIS

00:04:13.720 --> 00:04:19.640
From 2013 to 2016, Sirtis played a recurring
role on the police procedural drama series

00:04:19.640 --> 00:04:23.280
NCIS as Mossad director Orli Elbaz.

00:04:23.420 --> 00:04:28.840
Elbaz takes over the position as Israel's
top spy in the show's tenth season, and subsequently

00:04:28.840 --> 00:04:33.040
appears in episodes during season 11 and the
season 13 finale.

00:04:33.400 --> 00:04:38.020
According to Sirtis, she didn't have to read
for the role and was thrilled to have been

00:04:38.020 --> 00:04:38.820
offered the part.

00:04:38.920 --> 00:04:40.360
Sirtis told the A.V.

00:04:40.360 --> 00:04:40.860
Club,

00:04:40.860 --> 00:04:42.280
"I love to play strong women.

00:04:42.280 --> 00:04:43.080
I love it.

00:04:43.220 --> 00:04:44.380
Because that’s who I am.

00:04:44.460 --> 00:04:46.560
And [she] can kick anyone’s ass."

00:04:46.920 --> 00:04:48.900
New life and new civilizations

00:04:49.320 --> 00:04:52.320
Sirtis is showing no signs of slowing down.

00:04:52.320 --> 00:04:58.379
Notwithstanding her time travelling adventures
in Sharknado 6: The Last Sharknado, or appearing

00:04:58.379 --> 00:05:03.430
in Little Dead Rotting Hood, she's signed
on for a second season episode of The Orville,

00:05:03.430 --> 00:05:05.940
Seth Macfarlane's sci-fi comedy on Fox.

00:05:06.040 --> 00:05:11.880
Not coincidentally her episode will also be
directed by fellow Next Gen alum, and former

00:05:11.880 --> 00:05:14.220
on-screen boyfriend, Jonathan Frakes.

00:05:14.340 --> 00:05:20.300
More than any other Next Gen star, Sirtis
seems willing to put on her Starfleet uniform

00:05:20.309 --> 00:05:25.680
again and again, almost assuring fans that
we'll be seeing her again as Deanna Troi in

00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:30.240
CBS' upcoming series based on fan-favorite
Captain Jean-Luc Picard.

00:05:30.440 --> 00:05:30.940
"Make it so."

00:05:31.900 --> 00:05:32.400
"Sir?"

00:05:35.260 --> 00:05:35.900
"Do it."

